                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5634227e-4cc4-35d1-b758-c50d968670fe",
                        "entry_id": "89c4715e-7087-3511-bced-9a86cb5d6eef",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Propre ou relatif à Herman Melville et à son œuvre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9eb1175-3b42-47aa-a8f8-d4106ea1f2f7",
                                "sense_id": "5634227e-4cc4-35d1-b758-c50d968670fe",
                                "text": "Partant du maître livre melvillien, \"Moby Dick\", nous remonterons donc aux premiers écrits vis-à-vis desquels ce roman marque une rupture plus franchement subversive …."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ecdac82a-487e-4d89-98fa-279f53c1473f",
                                "sense_id": "5634227e-4cc4-35d1-b758-c50d968670fe",
                                "text": "Un des aspects les plus impressionnants de cet humour melvillien, c’est son énorme et déconcertante naïveté, sa terrifiante, son élémentaire simplicité de bouffonnerie, qui reste aussi imperturbable devant les flèches de la facétie que le front massif de Moby Dick elle-même."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "40345d00-8564-48d7-b60a-543d142e932f",
                        "source_entry_id": "89c4715e-7087-3511-bced-9a86cb5d6eef",
                        "source_sense_id": "5634227e-4cc4-35d1-b758-c50d968670fe",
                        "target_lang_word": "Melvillian",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Melvillian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0fbd6465-a77b-381d-9653-cecfdd98ec68",
                                        "entry_id": "a54179b6-e6d0-312b-8b6e-d20263909f78",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of Melvillean."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "139b35b9-d960-4ae7-8cd8-bfe5d47320c0",
                                                "sense_id": "0fbd6465-a77b-381d-9653-cecfdd98ec68",
                                                "text": "\"Then he rallied in Huntersville with Maricopa County (Ariz.) Sheriff Joe Arpaio, a Melvillian character on a never-ending crusade against Latinos.\"https://web.archive.org/web/20120529071053/http://www.charlotteobserver.com/2012/05/03/3217068/2-better-choices-in-9th-congressional.html"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Melvillian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7ffa2cc8-832f-3b88-b1f7-96641467b4d2",
                                        "entry_id": "d852c805-fa15-3fbf-a3fc-350b628fdf92",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of Melvillean."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "352d0a84-bff7-44ea-b35c-b96a00896317",
                                                "sense_id": "7ffa2cc8-832f-3b88-b1f7-96641467b4d2",
                                                "text": "Perhaps you think I am “spitefully” sitting on a lot of secrets—facts unknown to you or other Melvillians—I don’t know of a single fact that is unknown to you.—Many of them facts from my collection are to be found in the Pierre footnotes; if they have not already been published by other Melvillians."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93cb86ad-46be-4f2d-81f7-c1148ee46cdc",
                                                "sense_id": "7ffa2cc8-832f-3b88-b1f7-96641467b4d2",
                                                "text": "The reduction of aristocratic power had been achieved only at the cost of conciliating the Melvillians in the Scottish Church and leaving episcopacy in limbo."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89ec9b35-3311-42a7-8218-454825392d21",
                                                "sense_id": "7ffa2cc8-832f-3b88-b1f7-96641467b4d2",
                                                "text": "In 1596, James had successfully undermined Edinburgh’s support for the Melvillians by threatening to remove council and law court from the capital."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e8edd19-7e87-4e73-914a-7b646c93cd88",
                                                "sense_id": "7ffa2cc8-832f-3b88-b1f7-96641467b4d2",
                                                "text": "It was easier for the Melvillians to write manifestos than to bring these structures into being. For most of the 1567–73 civil war, the Scots Church remained a strange hybrid, a half-finished Reformed Church alongside the still-functioning husk of its Catholic predecessor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60ce8d4b-4bea-4dd8-a39f-8d56c7b86a61",
                                                "sense_id": "7ffa2cc8-832f-3b88-b1f7-96641467b4d2",
                                                "text": "Most Melvillians have their own favorite impassioned lyrical moments in Moby-Dick prior to the marathon reading."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9aa9a551-728d-42be-afe2-2dc9beba4732",
                                                "sense_id": "7ffa2cc8-832f-3b88-b1f7-96641467b4d2",
                                                "text": "While Melville began as a highly popular author, his fiction quickly fell into disfavor in the early 1850s. Most modern Melvillians have explained that descent by depicting Melville as the quintessentially brilliant but misunderstood writer, who grew increasingly alienated from and disdainful of his contemporary readers because they failed to respond to and appreciate the genius and complexity of his novels."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
